From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:48:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: bq27xxx: Report discharging at full charge too
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The gauge keeps its full-charge flag set after the input goes away or no
longer covers the load, so a pack at 100 % that is supplying the system
reports Full while its current is negative. User space then shows the
device as on external power.

Check the current first: a negative current is Discharging whatever the
flags say. Full is reported only when the pack is not discharging.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 0dd7ae0c (J71t ledger 6.14); made generic in bq27xxx_battery_current_and_status() instead of a J71t compatible check with a lookup of the "usb" supply]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
index e212572e2..766fa3e20 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
@@ -1976,12 +1976,13 @@ static int bq27xxx_battery_current_and_status(
 		val_curr->intval = curr;
 
 	if (val_status) {
-		if (bq27xxx_battery_is_full(di, flags))
+		/* A full flag describes capacity, not whether the pack supplies power. */
+		if (curr < 0)
+			val_status->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
+		else if (bq27xxx_battery_is_full(di, flags))
 			val_status->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
 		else if (curr > 0)
 			val_status->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
-		else if (curr < 0)
-			val_status->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
 		else
 			val_status->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
 	}
